This project builds on DrugBAN and reuses parts of its architecture and,
where the `dgl` backend is selected, its encoder implementations.

  DrugBAN
  Copyright (c) 2022 peizhenbai
  Licensed under the MIT License
  https://github.com/peizhenbai/DrugBAN

  Bai, P., Miljkovic, F., John, B. & Lu, H. "Interpretable bilinear attention
  network with domain adaptation improves drug-target prediction."
  Nature Machine Intelligence 5, 126-136 (2023).
  https://doi.org/10.1038/s42256-022-00605-1

The alpha-entmax projection in `ib_layer.py` is an independent
reimplementation of the method described in:

  Peters, B., Niculae, V. & Martins, A. F. T. "Sparse Sequence-to-Sequence
  Models." ACL 2019. https://arxiv.org/abs/1905.05702

Datasets fetched by `download_data.py` are redistributed by their original
authors under their own terms and are NOT covered by this license:

  Davis / KIBA   via the DeepDTA release
                 Ozturk, H., Ozgur, A. & Ozkirimli, E. "DeepDTA: deep
                 drug-target binding affinity prediction."
                 Bioinformatics 34(17), i821-i829 (2018).
                 https://github.com/hkmztrk/DeepDTA

  BindingDB /    via the DrugBAN release (MIT), originally derived from
  BioSNAP /      BindingDB, BioSNAP and the Human dataset of Liu et al.
  Human          https://github.com/peizhenbai/DrugBAN
